{"step_index":62,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T03:20:25Z","input_tokens":212,"cache_read_tokens":50688,"output_tokens":768,"content":"**\"Contribution timeline\"** is mounted — 83 real daily data points, zero interpolation.\n\n## How \"Actual Contribution\" Was Measured\n\nYou were right that raw commit count and raw line count are both misleading. Here's the exact pipeline:\n\n### Step 1 — Excluded noise files (proven, not asserted)\n| Excluded file | Lines removed |\n|---|---:|\n| `package-lock.json` | 20,044 |\n| `pnpm-lock.yaml` | 19,720 |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | 582 |\n| `pnpm-workspace.yaml` | 264 |\n| `hosted-providers.generated.ts` | 188 |\n| SVG/icon assets | 2 each |\n\nAlso excluded: `*.lock`, `*.snap`, `__snapshots__/`, `*.min.js|css`, `dist/`, `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, binaries (png/jpg/gif/ico/svg/fonts/pdf/zip/mp4).\n\n**~40,800 pure-noise lines stripped** → from raw ~1,052,000 down to **1,011,412 real lines**.\n\n### Step 2 — Excluded non-human authors\n`dependabot[bot]`, `github-actions`, `agor-discord` (release bot), any `*bot*`. Also excluded **merge commits** (`--no-merges`) so the same lines aren't counted twice.\n\n### Step 3 — The metric\n```\ncontribution_level = 0.5 × commits + 0.5 × log2(1 + real_lines)\n```\n- **`log2` is the key anti-lockfile guard.** Without it, a 61,850-line day (Oct 6) would dwarf every other day and the chart would be a spike plus a flat line. Log compression keeps the *shape* of effort visible.\n- **Commits are only half-weighted** — you said don't judge by commit count alone, so volume can't dominate.\n- **Lines are half-weighted** — because large lines alone (like the Oct 6 61,850-line commit) can be a single big feature, not proportional effort.\n\n### Step 4 — Verified against a second signal\nA commit-type weighted score (feat=1.0, fix=1.0, perf=0.9, refactor=0.8, test=0.7, docs=0.5, chore=0.3) produced the **same leaderboard ordering**: Maxime (363k) → Kamil (267k) → Richard (120k) → Kasia (76k) → Amin (30k). Two independent methods agreeing is the sanity check.\n\n## Timeline Read\n\n- **Peak: Aug 20 (17.86)** — 21 commits, 27k real lines: the highest-effort single day\n- **Second peak: Oct 8 (17.68)** — 20 commits / 42k lines\n- **Trough: Oct 10 (2.08)** — 1 commit, 8 real lines\n- **Clear mid-September lull** (Sep 10–21, mostly 5–9) then a strong **late-Sept/early-Oct ramp**\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: **Oct 6's 61,850 real lines in 13 commits** is unusually dense even after filtering — worth a glance to confirm it wasn't a large generated file that slipped the pattern (e.g. a migration dump or a big fixture).\n\nWant me to drill into that Oct 6 commit, or add author-level multi-line series on top of this?"}
